-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source tree depends on third-party open-source software (declared in
pyproject.toml) and the distributed container images bundle additional
components. Each such component remains under its own license; this NOTICE
does not relicense them.

The core path -- PostgreSQL, Apache AGE, pgvector, NATS, Cerbos, SpiceDB,
Sigstore cosign/Rekor, and the Python runtime dependencies -- is Apache-2.0,
MIT, BSD, or the PostgreSQL License, with the exception of the psycopg family
(psycopg, psycopg-binary, psycopg-pool), which is LGPL-3.0-only and is used as
an unmodified library. Several of these are themselves Apache-2.0 works that
ship their own NOTICE text (notably Apache AGE); those notices are carried by
the upstream artifacts the images are built from.

A machine-readable inventory of every bundled component and its license is
produced as CycloneDX and SPDX SBOMs on every CI run and every release:

  * source dependencies  -> sbom.cyclonedx.json, sbom.spdx.json
                            (.github/workflows/security.yml)
  * container image       -> sbom-container.cyclonedx.json (.github/workflows/security.yml,
                                                            release.yml)
  * license expressions   -> license-report.json (the license-scan CI job;
                            scripts/license_gate.py enforces the policy that
                            no strong-copyleft license enters the runtime
                            closure)

Consult those SBOM artifacts for the authoritative, version-pinned list of
third-party software and licenses in any given build.

Satellite systems integrated over the network (Wazuh, OpenCTI, MISP,
OpenSearch, MinIO, Netbox, Prometheus, Keycloak) carry their own licenses
(including GPL and AGPL) and operate as external services. core-graph
communicates with them through the ingest adapter pattern; their code is not
embedded in this redistributable source tree or in the core container images.
